# Run the Program

When the user says **Run the Program** (any casing), do this automatically — do not ask first. Finish only after all reachable endpoints work together.

From this repo root:

1. Start what is down: `npm run db:up`, then `npm run start:localhost` (API+web HTTPS+quick tunnel). Keep processes running.
2. Verify **together** (HTTP 200 / `/api/v1/health`):
 - Frontend (Local): https://localhost:3000
 - Frontend (LAN): https://192.168.1.69:3000
 - Frontend (Public): URL in `.public-url.txt` (quick-tunnel host changes each start). Also try any URL the user named.
 - Backend API: http://localhost:3001/api/v1/health
 - Backend API (LAN): http://192.168.1.69:3001/api/v1/health
3. Also hit `/api/v1/health` via localhost:3000 and the public origin (Next rewrite).
4. Keep cloudflared forwarding `https://127.0.0.1:3000` (`--no-tls-verify`). If the tunnel is down, restart it. Free trycloudflare hostnames cannot be reused after they die — publish the new URL.
5. Smoke Login plus Attendance, Dashboard, Leave, Payroll, Reports, Settings APIs. Fix CORS/routing/startup without breaking features.
6. Reply with pass/fail per URL, the live public link, and login: `admin@eitf.in` / `Admin@123` (Super Admin). Do not recreate demo users.
